  "tier": "told-once",
  "plain": "On March 25, 1948, girls riding horses toward Hart Canyon outside Aztec, New Mexico, are said to have been stopped and sent back, on the same day a flying saucer reportedly came down there. Scott Ramsey, who has spent years interviewing people about the Aztec case, says one of the women told him this. When he asked how she could be sure of the date, she said: \"Cuz it was my birthday.\" If true, it would put the crash and a guarded roadblock on a fixed day."
}
